= Conclusion <sec:conclusion>

Five chapters in, the argument is short enough to fit in one
paragraph: the value of a writing tool that builds AI in from the
start is not that it writes for you, but that it lets you delegate
the mechanical parts cleanly enough that you can focus on what only
you can do — having something worth saying.

== A workflow recap

If we had to compress the practical advice from this document into
five steps, it would be this:

+ *Read* the sources before you cite them. AI does not change this.
+ *Structure* the argument yourself, in your own outline. Ask the
  assistant for second-pass critique, not first-pass generation.
+ *Draft* in your own voice. Fix tone and tightness in revision —
  this is where AI assistance pays off most.
+ *Verify* every citation, especially ones the AI surfaced.
  Resolving the DOI takes ten seconds and prevents most disasters.
+ *Disclose* AI use according to the venue's policy. When in doubt,
  err toward transparency.

